  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "Find the final intensity of light (I\"), if the angle between the axes of two polaroids is $60^{\\circ}$.\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/F85G7OkNKzViqzZ2bu3CPqzm_WQWtzvg3XO4_m1fGKU.original.fullsize.png\">",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "AUNDu",
      "text": "$\\frac{3 \\mathrm{I}_{0}}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "k6dEV",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{I}_{0}}{2}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0qiQH",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{I}_{0}}{4}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wuYW2",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\mathrm{I}_{0}}{8}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "From the first polaroid\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\mathrm{I}^{\\prime}=\\frac{\\mathrm{I}_{0}}{2}\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\nFrom second polaroid\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n\\begin{aligned}\r\n\r\n\\mathrm{I}^{\\prime \\prime} &=\\mathrm{I}^{\\prime} \\cos ^{2} \\theta=\\frac{\\mathrm{I}_{0}}{2} \\cos ^{2}\\left(60^{\\circ}\\right) \\\\\r\n\r\n&=\\frac{\\mathrm{I}_{0}}{2} \\times\\left(\\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{2}=\\frac{\\mathrm{I}_{0}}{8}\r\n\r\n\\end{aligned}\r\n\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
